ExifTool
--------

ExifTool (https://exiftool.org), by Phil Harvey, is an external program run by
MediaRenamer through a subprocess. It is installed manually by the user in
`bin/` (e.g. `bin/exiftool-13.62_64/`), on the PATH or through EXIFTOOL_PATH,
and is NOT redistributed in this repository (`bin/` is git-ignored). It remains
under its own license: free software, redistributable and modifiable under the
same terms as Perl itself (Perl Artistic License or GNU GPL).

If an ExifTool binary is ever redistributed with MediaRenamer, add its notices
and license text here or in `LICENSES/`.

Python packages
---------------

No third-party Python package is required by the program itself (standard
library only). `uv sync` installs, from PyPI, a development tool and an
optional helper that are not redistributed here and keep their own licenses:

- pytest (MIT license) and its dependencies, for the tests;
- tzdata (Apache License 2.0), optional, the IANA time zone database for
  Windows, which has none; without it only time zone features are disabled.
